as a visually distinct structural abnormality consistent with a tumor pattern.\n\n**X-AI summary**\n- **Confidence interpretation:** the model output is very high-confidence, but the tool itself explicitly says imaging analysis is **not definitive diagnostic proof**.\n- **Summary:** the pipeline judged the image as having a **high likelihood of kidney cancer**, based on tumor-like visual features.\n- **Visual evidence:** it detected a kidney tumor pattern in the scan.\n- **Recommended next steps:**\n  1. Further medical evaluation with imaging and lab testing\n  2. Prompt discussion with a medical professional\n  3. Consideration of further diagnostic workup if needed\n\n**Clinical interpretation**\nThis tool output is **consistent with your already documented kidney cancer history**, and it does **not reduce the urgency** created by your current symptoms: **worsening right flank pain, blood in urine, burning urination, and recent fever**. Those symptoms still need **same-day medical evaluation**, because infection, obstruction, bleeding, or cancer-related complications can all be important here.\n\n**What I recommend now**\n- **Seek same-day urgent medical care today**\n- If possible, contact your **oncology/urology team immediately**\n- If fever worsens, pain becomes severe, urine output drops, you vomit, feel weak/dizzy, or bleeding increases, go to the **ER**\n\nIf you want, I can next do one of these:\n1. write you a **short urgent message** to send to your specialist right now  \n2. help you use the **LLM distillation** step to turn all of this into a clean medical summary  \n3. give you a **combined interpretation** of your symptoms + EHR + this pipeline result\n\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04a478fd4d551a920169bc220b9fa08191908c5b4a89b278f1\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"